<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guillaume du Tillot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1711–1774</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Léon Guillaume du Tillot</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guillaume du Tillot (1711–1774) was a French-born statesman who served as chief minister of the Duchy of Parma under Duke Philip and his son Ferdinand. An <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment">Enlightenment</a> reformer, he limited clerical privileges, expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a> in 1768, promoted manufacturing and founded the Palatine Library. He was dismissed in 1771.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guillaume-du-tillot.jpg" alt="Guillaume du Tillot" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pietro Melchiorre Ferrari · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ferrari_-_Guillaume_du_Tillot_-_Biblioteca_Palatina,_Parma.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
